// SALTMARCH - the conversation an entity's 'talk' verb runs.
//
// Nothing here is new machinery. This is the Phase W runtime, unchanged, reached by a verb an
// author permitted on an entity rather than by a cue fired inside a fight - which is the whole of
// what "interactions lean on the dialogue runtime" means (PLACES_AND_PERSISTENCE.md section 12).
//
// Two rules, both enforced by the loader, both unchanged from greyhollow:
//
//   1. Every line carries an explicit #line: tag, which becomes the last segment of its key.
//   2. The text below is the author's working copy and is never what a player reads. The words
//      come from locale/saltmarch.csv, in every language including English.

title: norrel_at_the_quay
speaker: wolf
---
The man on the boards has been waiting for somebody all morning. #line:waiting_all_morning
He wants the sluice at the weir opened, and he will not say why. #line:will_not_say_why

-> Ask what is at the weir #line:ask_what_is_at_the_weir
    Jacks. Two, he thinks. He is being careful with the number. #line:careful_with_the_number
    <<jump the_errand_itself>>
-> Ask why he will not go himself #line:ask_why_not_himself
    Because he is a man who hires. That is not a crime, whatever your face is doing. #line:a_man_who_hires
    <<jump the_errand_itself>>
===

title: the_errand_itself
speaker: wolf
---
Open the gate, come back, and he pays. #line:open_it_and_come_back
He has to be here to pay you, mind. Do try to remember that. #line:has_to_be_here_to_pay
===
